ency Department, OP: Operative Procedure, and RAD: Radiology) and all reports combined in the test set as applied by the ConText algorithm in the test set. Each cell contains up to three trigger terms, each of which is followed by the number of instances in which that trigger term was used by ConText to change the default value of a contextual property to the value given in the first row. The number of unique trigger terms (<italic toggle="yes">Unique)</italic> refers to the total number of different trigger terms found in the test set. For example, for Operative Procedure reports we list the three most frequent trigger terms for the value <italic toggle="yes">negated</italic> (“no”, “no evidence of”, and “free”), but two other trigger terms (namely, “not” and “with no”) were also used for a total of five unique trigger terms.</p></caption><table frame="box" rules="cols"><thead><tr><th valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="2" valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1">negated</th><th colspan="2" valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1">historical</th><th colspan="2" valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1">hypothetical</th><th colspan="2" valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1">Other</th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="bottom" colspan="9" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">SP</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No evidence of</td><td align="right" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">History</td><td align="right" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="right" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="right" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No</td><td